# The frozen graph is ground truth and is cited by sha256 throughout the docs.
# Line-ending translation on checkout would change that hash, which defeats the
# entire point of citing it. Store and emit these bytes exactly as written.
data/*.json -text

# Same reasoning, wider scope. Every generated artifact below is written with an
# explicit newline="\n" by its generator (tools/snapshot_weights.py,
# tools/snapshot_tests.py, tools/run_h5_h6.py). If git translates on checkout,
# a cloner's bytes differ from what the generator produces: results/h5_h6.json
# is cited by sha256, and the snapshots would diff whole-file on every
# regeneration, which destroys the "read the diff as a report" convention.
#
# Added 2026-08-10 after git warned "LF will be replaced by CRLF" on all three.
# This is the frozen-graph hash defect recurring in a new place, so the rule is
# written against the class rather than the one file that triggered it.
results/*.json -text
tests/*.json -text
